            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I've implemented `ext_images` in [Zonvie](https://github.com/akiyosi/zonvie) (macOS/Windows GUI): akiyosi/zonvie#36. The protocol was straightforward to implement, and virtual\r\nplacements integrate very naturally with a grid renderer. Three notes:\r\n\r\n1. **GUIs can't report their cell size.** With no tty UI, `cell_as_pixel_size()` falls back to 10x20 (aspect 2.0), so auto-sized images are distorted in every GUI — mine are ~11%\r\nstretched (cells 17.94x39.88 px). Could a UI report its cell pixel size, e.g. via a UI option?\r\n2. **Direct-placement stacking vs text/floats/cursor is unspecified** — it decides whether a UI can use a simple top-layer overlay or must composite into the grid. An explicit\r\nstatement either way would help.\r\n3. Doc nit: \"intrinsic image size\" is ambiguous on HiDPI (device px vs points).\r\n\r\nHappy to test protocol changes (e.g. chunked `img_data`) as this evolves.\r\n",
